Borrowed from Panthera Speech
-----------------------------

Two things the SAPI 5 server in `sapi5/` does were learned from Panthera
Speech by Tamas Geczy, which presents the Apple voices of Tiger through Lion
to SAPI and NVDA:

    https://github.com/tgeczy/panthera-speech

The first is that a bookmark fragment's text is the bookmark's *name* rather
than words to speak, and that JAWS sends every word as its own fragment with
a bookmark between each pair -- so an engine that appends fragment text
blindly reads the bookmark names aloud, and one that drops them without
restoring a space runs the neighbouring words together.  The second is that
NVDA's SAPI driver interleaves bookmarks with the text and waits for the
events before advancing, so an engine that never posts them stalls.  Neither
is in any specification; both are in Panthera's source as comments earned
against real clients.

